+/**
+ * @file        ui/vulkan/vulkan_presenter_framegen.cpp
+ * @brief       wwe2k16 patch: frame generation for the Vulkan presenter (present_frame_generation).
+ *
+ * For every new guest frame the presenter first shows an in-between frame made from it and the previous one, then the
+ * frame itself half a frame interval later (Presenter::ScheduleFrameGenRepaint). A game rendering 40 frames a second
+ * is shown at up to 80 on a 90 / 120 Hz screen; input still acts at the game's rate, and the real frame is shown
+ * about half a frame later than without.
+ *
+ * The in-between frame (all GPU, in the paint's own command buffer, before the guest output is drawn):
+ *   1. frame_gen_downsample.comp  the previous and current frame's luma at a quarter of the size (rgba16f, packed)
+ *   2. frame_gen_motion.comp      a motion vector per 16x16 pixels, searched symmetrically from the in-between time
+ *                                 (coarse steps of 2 quarter-size texels, then +-1; a small bias to short vectors)
+ *   3. frame_gen_interpolate.frag per pixel, the best of its block's and the 4 neighbouring blocks' vectors (the pair
+ *                                 of half-warped samples that agree best), blended with a plain mix where none fits
+ *   4. the same shader in copy mode: the current frame into the other history image (the previous one next time)
+ * Two history images alternate, so a pass never writes an image that the same paint reads.
+ *
+ * Skipped (the real frame is painted as usual): the first frame, a size change, frames further apart than
+ * present_frame_generation_max_gap_ms (loads, pauses, menus that wait), and a frame that comes before the pending real
+ * one was shown (the game is at or above half the display rate: nothing to gain).
+ *
+ * @license     BSD 3-Clause License (as the SDK)
+ */
+
